:"Flash Flood Warning issued August 15 at 2:55PM MDT until August 15 at 4:45PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"At 255 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms had moved out of\nthe warned area. Between 1 and 2 inches of rain have fallen. Flooding\nimpacts will continue, but no additional rainfall is expected. Flash\nflooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, gulches, roads,\nand poor drainage and low-lying areas.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nMainly rural areas of Southeastern Douglas County.\n\nThis includes the following streams and drainages...\nCarpenter Creek, Cherry Creek, West Cherry Creek, East Cherry\nCreek, Antelope Creek, Crowfoot Creek and Lake Gulch.","ends":"2026-08-15T16:45:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Douglas, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ca1f71633652faed8c8d9e2ccf220db3a3a34f64.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ca1f71633652faed8c8d9e2ccf220db3a3a34f64.001.1"},{"event":"Severe Thunderstorm Watch","headline":"Severe Thunderstorm Watch issued August 15 at 2:05PM MDT until August 15 at 9:00PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"THE NATIONAL WEATHER SERVICE HAS ISSUED SEVERE THUNDERSTORM WATCH\n584 IN EFFECT UNTIL 9 PM MDT THIS EVENING FOR THE FOLLOWING AREAS\n\nIN COLORADO THIS WATCH INCLUDES 9 COUNTIES\n\nIN EAST CENTRAL COLORADO\n\nELBERT                LINCOLN\n\nIN NORTHEAST COLORADO\n\nADAMS                 ARAPAHOE              DOUGLAS\nLOGAN                 MORGAN                WASHINGTON\nWELD\n\nTHIS INCLUDES THE CITIES OF AKRON, AURORA, CASTLE ROCK,\nCENTENNIAL, ELIZABETH, FORT MORGAN, GREELEY, KIOWA, LIMON,\nPARKER, STERLING, THORNTON, WESTMINSTER, AND WINDSOR.","ends":"2026-08-15T21:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Adams, CO; Arapahoe, CO; Douglas, CO; Elbert, CO; Lincoln, CO; Logan, CO; Morgan, CO; Washington, CO; Weld, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.862838f8b61c9032ddaddac2ecfc011791cca58a.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.862838f8b61c9032ddaddac2ecfc011791cca58a.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued August 15 at 11:52AM MDT until August 15 at 10:00PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Flash Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of central and northeast Colorado, including the\nfollowing areas: the southern Front Range Foothills, Palmer Divide\narea, I-25 corridor, and all of our eastern plains counties.\n\n* WHEN...Until 10 PM MDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nFlooding may occur in poor drainage and urban areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Additional thunderstorms and heavy rainfall this afternoon,\ncombined with the heavy rainfall from the past 3 days, will bring\na threat for flash flooding this afternoon and evening. Stronger\nstorms will be capable of producing 1 to 2 inches of rain in 30\nminutes, with isolated areas receiving storm totals of 2 to 4\ninches.","ends":"2026-08-15T22:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Jefferson and West Douglas Counties Above  6000 Feet/Gilpin/Clear Creek/Northeast Park Counties Below 9000 Feet; Larimer County Below 6000 Feet/Northwest Weld County; Boulder And Jefferson Counties Below 6000 Feet/West Broomfield County; North Douglas County Below 6000 Feet/Denver/West Adams and Arapahoe Counties/East Broomfield County; Elbert/Central and East Douglas Counties Above 6000 Feet; Northeast Weld County; Central and South Weld County; Morgan County; Central and East Adams and Arapahoe Counties; North and Northeast Elbert County Below 6000 Feet/North Lincoln County; Southeast Elbert County Below 6000 Feet/South Lincoln County; Logan County; Washington County; Sedgwick County; Phillips County",